        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Graves, Dino Buzzati\n- Works: The White Goddess\n- Roles: poet, novelist, critic, classicist, short story writer, painter, journalist\n- Organizations: Corriere della Sera\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Graves, born Robert von Ranke Graves on 24 July 1895 and died on 7 December 1985, was an English poet, novelist, critic, and classicist.\n- Dino Buzzati-Traverso, born on 14 October 1906 and died on 28 January 1972, was an Italian novelist, short story writer, painter, poet, and journalist for Corriere della Sera.\n- The White Goddess: a Historical Grammar of Poetic Myth is a book-length essay by Robert Graves about the nature of poetic myth-making.",
